      "verified_by": "A-ROOT-IDENTIFIER-LENGTH-NONNEGATIVE",
      "fine_trace_step": 4,
      "description": "Root cause. `ParseIdentifier()` only rejects `length == -1` or a positive length that exceeds the remaining string. With the witness, `length == -9`; `AtLeastNumCharsRemaining(..., -9)` returns true because its loop never executes for a negative bound, so the function accepts a negative identifier length instead of rejecting it."
    },
